{"title":"Career Roadmap — R&D Engineer","role":"R&D Engineer","summary":"A Micro & Nano Electronics R&D Engineer develops, tests, characterizes, and improves electronic devices, circuits, semiconductor technologies, sensors, and nanoscale systems.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Micro & Nano Electronics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Micro & Nano Electronics R&D Engineer develops, tests, characterizes, and improves electronic devices, circuits, semiconductor technologies, sensors, and nanoscale systems."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Semiconductor physics"},{"text":"Microelectronics"},{"text":"VLSI"},{"text":"Analog and digital electronics"},{"text":"Device physics"},{"text":"Nanoelectronics"},{"text":"Semiconductor fabrication"},{"text":"Circuit simulation"},{"text":"Device characterization"},{"text":"Embedded/computational methods"},{"text":"Research and experimental engineering"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical R&D environments include semiconductor companies, electronics manufacturers, chip-design organizations, research laboratories, universities, sensor companies, MEMS organizations, and advanced technology startups."},{"type":"p","text":"For a student targeting advanced semiconductor research, M.Tech/M.E. or a research-focused Master's/Ph.D. can significantly improve access to specialized R&D positions, although bachelor's graduates can enter junior engineering and test/characterization roles."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Main Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Tech Micro/Nano Electronics"},{"text":"Electronics + semiconductor + device fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Junior R&D / Device Engineer"},{"text":"Simulation + characterization + experiments"}],[{"text":"2033–2037"},{"text":"R&D Engin